 "title": "core", "category": "Framework", "author": "irpina, Iced-Cream",
 "description": "The boot copier, the hook bus, mod storage and parameter pages for the Analog Rytm MKII: every other mod needs it. The Digitakt mk1's core.s, settings.s and render.s with the Rytm's addresses, and store.c: fields mods declare, placed by elekloader from the build's lockfile and kept in bytes stock never uses or always holds at 0; and pages.s: parameter pages and parameter overrides mods add through the tables core_pages and core_params (and core_page_fns, a page whose knobs follow the sound), from the first instructions of the four routines a page goes through, and the page keys' lists, stock's pages and then the ones mods add through core_view_pages, which the page key steps through (skipping a page while its mod says it is hidden, with the page's title in the header), and which keeps its page when the view is shown again; load.s: the audio interrupt's load, core_audio_load, for mods with work they can skip; and machines.c: machines mods add in the hidden slots 34..43 through core_machines, written into the machine table and the slots' parameter records at boot. On its own it changes nothing the unit does.",
 "device": "analog-rytm-mk2", "os": "1.74",
 "sources": ["../core/core.s", "../core/settings.s", "../core/render.s", "store.c", "store.s", "route.s", "pages.s", "load.s", "machines.c"],
